{"prior":"<p>Qwen turns an issue and candidate files into vectors. Flix compares those vectors and orders the files. The browser shows saved results; these controls do not run inference.</p><section class=\"code-walk\" data-walk=\"cosine\"></section><section class=\"code-walk\" data-walk=\"vectors\"></section><h3>Break exact ties by path</h3><p>The same score need not mean the same file. This comparator keeps ordering deterministic: greater similarity first, then ascending path.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/scoreOrder.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Study/Embedding.flix:153–163</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"153\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">similarityOrder</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(left: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Scored</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, right: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Scored</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Comparison</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"154\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> leftPath = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">fst</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(left);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"155\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> leftScore = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">snd</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(left);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"156\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> rightPath = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">fst</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(right);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"157\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">let</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> rightScore = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">snd</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(right);</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"158\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (leftScore &gt; rightScore) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Comparison</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">LessThan</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"159\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (leftScore &lt; rightScore) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Comparison</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">GreaterThan</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"160\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (leftPath &lt; rightPath) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Comparison</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">LessThan</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"161\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (leftPath &gt; rightPath) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Comparison</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">GreaterThan</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"162\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Comparison</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">EqualTo</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"163\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    }</span></span></code></pre></figure><pre class=\"pattern-diagram\"><code class=\"language-text\">&lt;file, score&gt;\n    |\n    +-- unequal scores ==&gt; larger score first\n    |\n    `-- equal scores ===&gt; earlier path first\n</code></pre><h3>Read the saved outcome</h3><p>Jev sees the first 32 candidates. It cannot promote a file that Qwen left below that boundary. This table contains historical results for the selected issue.</p><figure class=\"inline-graph\" data-mini=\"ranks\"></figure><!--MechanismEvidence-->","atlas":"<p>Atlas records files, symbols and resolved connections in a pinned source world. A typed expression asks one precise question about those connections.</p><!--MechanismEvidence--><h3>Check the shared positions</h3><p>Every shared position must mean one kind of entity. This check rejects a position used as both a File and a Symbol.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/domains.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:275–285</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"275\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// One role slot must mean one nominal domain. The domains come from the core</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"276\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// signature table, so an atom that reads a role as a file and an atom that</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"277\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// writes it as a symbol cannot be composed into one conjunction.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"278\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsConsistent</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">AtomPattern</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">]): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Bool</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"279\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">forAll</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(role -&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">length</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">distinct</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsOf</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(role, atoms))) &lt;= </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">distinct</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">roleList</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atoms)))</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"280\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"281\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">domainsOf</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(role: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, atoms: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">AtomPattern</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">]): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Domain</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">] =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"282\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">List</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">flatMap</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom -&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"283\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            (</span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (atom#subject == role) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Attune</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">atomSource</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom#relation) :: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"284\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">                ::: (</span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (atom#object == role) </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Attune</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">atomTarget</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(atom#relation) :: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Nil</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">),</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"285\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            atoms)</span></span></code></pre></figure><section class=\"code-walk\" data-walk=\"anchor\"></section><h3>Give equivalent questions the same identity</h3><p>Role numbers are placeholders. Consistently renaming them must not create a new structural question. Canonicalization sorts, removes duplicates and renumbers the description before computing its identity.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/canonical.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Theory.flix:302–313</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"302\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The canonical descriptor: the least of the consistent renamings, with the</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"303\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// atoms sorted and de-duplicated and the roles renumbered by first</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"304\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// appearance.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"305\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">canonical</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"306\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">match</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">bestOption</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate, </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">renamings</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(), </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">None</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"307\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">case</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">None</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">         =&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">emptyDescriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"308\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">            </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">case</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Some</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(option) =&gt; </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">renumber</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">renamed</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate, option))</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"309\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        }</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"310\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"311\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The canonical identity key. Two descriptors share it exactly when they are</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"312\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// the same candidate up to a consistent renaming of their role slots.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"313\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">identityKey</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Descriptor</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">String</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">render</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">canonical</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(candidate))</span></span></code></pre></figure><pre class=\"pattern-diagram\"><code class=\"language-text\">&lt;same relations, renamed slots&gt;\n                |\n                v\n           canonical\n                |\n                v\n       &lt;one descriptor identity&gt;\n</code></pre>","jev":"<p>Jev judges Qwen’s first 32 candidates. The input contains the issue prefix, paths and retrieval fields; the structural condition adds retained relation summaries and template IDs. It contains no source bodies.</p><pre class=\"pattern-diagram\"><code class=\"language-text\">&lt;issue + Qwen top 32&gt;\n    |\n    +-- QJ ==&gt; path + retrieval fields\n    |\n    `-- QS ==&gt; same fields + Atlas metadata\n                   |\n                   v\n        &lt;Relevant / NotRelevant / Unknown&gt;\n</code></pre><h3>Turn a judgment into an ordering key</h3><p>Relevant gets group 0. Every other outcome gets group 1. The original rank is the second part of the key.</p><figure class=\"source-window flix-reading\"><figcaption><a href=\"sources/promotion.flix\" download>attune/src/Attune/Study/Jev.flix:56–61</a> · actual source</figcaption><pre class=\"source-code\"><code><span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"56\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// Whether an outcome promotes its candidate. Only `Relevant` does.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"57\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">promotes</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(outcome: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">JevOutcome</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Bool</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> = outcome == </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">JevOutcome</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">.</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Relevant</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"58\"></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"59\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#A8939B\">/// The frozen stable promotion key `(Relevant ? 0 : 1, original base rank)`.</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"60\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">    </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">pub</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">def</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">promotionKey</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(outcome: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">JevOutcome</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, baseRank: </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">): (</span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, </span><span style=\"color:#CFB9DF\">Int32</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">) =</span></span>\n<span class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"61\"><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">        (</span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">if</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#EDCE96\">promotes</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">(outcome)) </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">0</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#DDA0B3\">else</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\"> </span><span style=\"color:#E6BB78\">1</span><span style=\"color:#F1E9D9\">, baseRank)</span></span></code></pre></figure><section class=\"code-walk\" data-walk=\"promote\"></section><h3>Read the saved outcome</h3><p>The table shows historical judgments and ranks. Correct structure can still accompany a wrong relevance decision.</p><figure class=\"inline-graph\" data-mini=\"ranks\"></figure><!--MechanismEvidence-->"}